 dict(id='doll-controlled-formula',Source_contract='L1MagicPc.calcNpcMagicDamage applies PC_TO_PET_DAMAGE_MULTIPLIER in magic calculation and IMMUNE_TO_HARM when active. L1PetInstance.receiveDamage/commitDamageState apply the received HP delta without a second pet multiplier. Raw proc bonus bypasses the magic formula.',implementation_gate='Controlled SKILL must use the existing companion magic calculation, bonus must remain raw. Full NPC immunity/buff consumers remain an explicit semantic gap requiring implementation/review; existing companion routing alone is not proof that every Source reduction is covered.'),
 dict(id='doll-slow-and-generic-skill',Source_contract='executeSkillProc always calculates/commits magic damage first, then target castgfx, matching doll aggression, and slow29 handling. calcMagicDiceDamage has a critical RNG plus original/equipment/talent magic contributions even for a skill with zero base dice; slow is not safely treated as zero-damage-only. handleSlowSkill applies slow to normal speed, cancels a recognized haste at speed1, and leaves already-slow/default speeds unchanged.',implementation_gate='Complete generic Source skill numerical/visual metadata and reuse the existing spell-damage order before implementing29. Do not charge normal spell MP/materials, add another ordinary probability test, skip Source critical RNG, refresh an existing slow lease, or present the doll aggression before target castgfx.'),
 dict(id='doll-proc-view-controls',Source_contract='SkillsTable fills actual skill_level/castgfx/dice/count; proc target sounds use radius10 with proc_spr enabled, using tile-line (Chebyshev) distance. Doll aggression67 uses all visible proc viewers. L1PcInstance defaults proc_spr to true.',implementation_gate='Preserve per-viewer preference, actual target coordinates, target-castgfx before doll aggression, role/source/life/receiver proof at final Frame, and default/reset behavior across role replacement. A constructor default and toggle alone do not complete role/reset/final-output qualification.'),
 dict(id='doll-nonblocking-child-events',Source_contract='DamageCommit.enqueue returns queue admission, not HP completion. DamageCommitQueue publishes the event and schedules a drainer; DamageCommitApplier invokes afterAccepted only after actual HP acceptance. executeSkillProc/UnifiedProcExecutor continue the skill loop and graphics without awaiting each nested child HP event.',implementation_gate='Preserve FIFO/admission/actual-HP guards and the Source nonblocking submission/effect order. Do not introduce synchronous child waits or a per-child continuation chain merely to force later procs/physical figures to await child acceptance; that would change Source semantics. Rejected events, fatality and final output remain validation dimensions.'),
 dict(id='doll-defense-accepted-and-zero',Source_contract='calcOnDefense rolls and sums DAMAGE_REDUCTION in Calc, stores its GFX, and receiveDamageInternal subtracts/clamps before enqueuing the independent HP event. processDamageCommit accepts even an unchanged zero-delta HP event and then applies defense side effects. reductionOnly preserves reduction GFX and the original one-use guard; broadcastDefenseProcGfx sends positive GFX around the victim radius10, otherwise matching original doll aggression67 to proc viewers.',implementation_gate='Retain the already existing native Calc RNG/value and accepted once/equipment tail. Freeze the original defender summon before waits, carry detached original-role/life/summon/audience proofs on the existing DefenseVisual, seal fatal life at actual HP acceptance, and revalidate the actual Frame receiver. Do not reroll defense, cancel ordinary HP when a cosmetic proof expires, or grant a replacement doll powers to an old action. Paths without a proven original Context remain an explicit coverage gap.'),
 dict(id='incoming-actual-attacker-kind',Source_contract='L1PcInstance.receiveDamageInternal wraps defense Calc and incoming-hit effects in attacker!=null, while equipped145/149 and Avatar scaling remain outside that branch. L1Cube supplies its actual effect NPC, so an effect source is not equivalent to null or its player owner. The retained native Fatality catalog labels its category and Heal weights as provisional compatibility policy.',implementation_gate='Classify each actual ingress as PC, owned/natural/effect NPC, genuinely no attacker or still unknown before adapting this branch. Inspect the current NativeCombatAttacker ingress as well as the Java caster argument. Do not disable NPC defense merely because the caster argument is null; do not borrow an ambient/player identity for an unbound effect. Fatality/null-source differences remain implementation work, not a fix established by this reference audit.'),
